<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maule River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Maule is a river of central Chile that flows from the Andes to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pacific-ocean">Pacific Ocean</a> at Constitución. Tradition holds that it marked the southern limit of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca Empire</a>, where Inca expansion stopped in the face of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mapuche">Mapuche</a> resistance in the late 15th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maule-river.jpg" alt="Maule River" width="320" height="481" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anaximander · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rio_Maule_aerial2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
